     "title": "💬 Dear Aunt Sally",
     "html": "<div class=\"ex\">I am very, very shy. I have just arrived in a new school and I am afraid to speak to the other students. When the teacher asks me a question, I go red. I stammer. — Jill (aged 15)</div><div class=\"ex\"><b>Dear Jill,</b> A lot of people are shy, but you can learn to be confident. Don’t hurry. It takes time.<br>1 Say to yourself, ‘I will speak to somebody today.’<br>2 Be friendly. Say ‘hello’ and smile.<br>3 Before you speak, count to five.<br>4 Ask your teacher to give you a little time to answer.</div>",
